+
+## What the current tests demonstrate
+
+Run `yarn test` for the address-derivation assertion, the existing Merkle and
+signature checks, and Foundry. `yarn test:practice` runs just the TypeScript
+checks through the already-installed `tsx` runner; no new dependency is needed.
+
+- Address derivation compares the manual result with viem using a deliberately
+  public demonstration fixture. Private keys and complete account objects are
+  not logged. Never fund or reuse demonstration accounts.
+- The Merkle exercise builds exactly four leaves and produces a proof for C.
+  Its check covers that proof, a changed value, a wrong sibling direction and
+  reordered leaves. General trees, every leaf position, odd lengths and an
+  explicit empty-input policy remain learner work.
+- Signature checks cover recovery, changed messages, raw versus EIP-191
+  digests and canonical low-s signatures. They do not establish a complete
+  transaction-signing or contract-verification implementation.
+- `Scaffold.t.sol` checks that the toolchain runs a trivial arithmetic assertion.
+  Contract behavior, authorization, accounting and adversarial tests remain
+  learner work; a green scaffold is not evidence that those labs are complete.
+
+Record the command, its result, the exact demonstrated scope and the next
+unproved claim in the lesson's Terrain note. Keep earlier reasoning and errors.
